.TH TOTHEFRONT 1
.SH NAME
tothefront \- hex-grid wargame
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/tothefront
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tothefront
is a port of the TempleOS hex-grid wargame
.IR ToTheFront .
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Two sides of 32 units (infantry, artillery, light and medium tanks)
fight on a randomly generated hex map of plains, woods, mountains,
rivers and roads.
At start-up the game prompts for a hex game seed and then asks,
for each player, whether that side is played by a human or by the
stock machine controller, so human-vs-human hotseat, human-vs-AI
on either side, and AI-vs-AI all work.
.PP
Each turn has six sub-phases with alternating initiative:
each player in turn plots artillery fire, moves, then fires directly.
Movement pays per-hex costs (roads are fast, woods and mountains slow,
rivers consume all movement, tanks pay to turn), and tanks face one
of six directions; armour protection depends on the attacker's bearing.
Direct fire rolls to-hit against accuracy, range, a woods penalty and
a high-ground bonus; artillery fire is plotted blind inside a range
circle, resolves at the end of the turn, scatters on a miss, and
blasts seven hexes.
Tanks overrun infantry and infantry close-assault tanks by moving
into their hex.
Line of sight is blocked by woods and mountains and hides unseen
enemy units from each player's view.
The full arithmetic of every attack is printed to a combat log.
The last side with units standing wins.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B LMB
Select a unit; release on a hex to plot, move, or fire
.TP
.B space / RMB
End the current phase
.TP
.B s
Toggle the line-of-sight overlay from the cursor hex
(the original holds SHIFT)
.TP
.B 1, 2
Show player 1's or player 2's view
.TP
.B c
View the combat odds log (Esc returns)
.TP
.B d
Set the animation delay
.TP
.B Enter
Start a new game
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/tothefront.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
